              text: 'Hold deposits A bank accepts and holds money ( deposits ) that people put into Deposits: Money placed in a bank account that can be withdrawn as per the terms of the bank and often earns interest. This account is for individuals who save regularly and earn interest on such savings. It opens with a minimum deposit and allows money to be added or withdrawn, though there are limits on how often the depositor can withdraw each month. Savings account This account is for businesses and traders who often make and receive payments. It doesn’t earn interest, but generally, there are no limits on how many times money can be deposited or withdrawn. Current account This is a one-time deposit kept for a fixed period, like or years. After that time, the bank returns the original amount, plus interest, which is usually higher than what a savings account offers. Fixed deposit account Fig. 8.4. Types of bank accounts Banks provide the following types of accounts: 29-11-2025 14:47:40 29-11-2025 14:47:40 Economic Life Around Us – Banks and the Magic of Finance the bank account. They not only keep it safe for us but also lend it to businesses or other people. In return, the banks give us some extra money over a regular period (say quarterly or monthly or annually) in the form of ‘ interest ’, which helps the amount of our money saved to grow over time. Through this, banks encourage individuals to save. Let us understand how your savings would significantly increase if you save for a long time. Imagine you get ₹1000 on your birthday from your mother.',
